## Step 3: RiScreenWindow, RiCropWindow and RiFrameAspectRatio together,
## under perspective. RiScreenWindow and RiCropWindow already have their
## own defect-regression fixtures (orthowindow.rib/cropwindow_test.cpp,
## fixed by the UAT-defects pass); this scene is the combination none of
## those isolated tests covers -- an asymmetric ScreenWindow shifting the
## visible frustum off-centre, then CropWindow rendering only a sub-window
## of that already-shifted result.
##
## RiFrameAspectRatio has no tokenizer entry at all (SPEC.md's "RIB
## support" table, "Unrecognized" bucket) -- included here to prove it is
## warned-and-skipped, not a parse-desync, and that ScreenWindow/CropWindow
## right after it still parse correctly (AGENTS.md's "desync convention").
Display "screenwindow.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 400 300 1
FrameAspectRatio 1.5
ScreenWindow -2 0.5 -0.75 0.75
CropWindow 0.25 0.75 0.0 1.0
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.3]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [5 0 0] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 1
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.9]
Sphere 1 -1 1 360
WorldEnd
